@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pti268-nouns`
IMPORT `pti268-definitions`
IMPORT `pti268-extensions`
IMPORT `pti268-conditions`
IMPORT `pti268-claims`
IMPORT `pti268-annex-transport`
IMPORT `pti268-fixtures`

-- Tests of the provisions one at a time: Part I (definitions), Part III (conditions that do
-- not need a whole claim), Part VI (extensions), Part VII (time limits and documents) and
-- the Annex. Each expected value is the source's figure or the arithmetic the source
-- prescribes, worked by hand beside the assertion before it was run; none was copied from an
-- evaluation. The schedule figures are the fixtures' scenario values. Both sides of every
-- threshold the provision states are tested.

§ `Tests — the provisions one at a time`

§§ `Part I — definitions`

-- def 1: a doctor who is the insured's spouse is not a "doctor".
#ASSERT `counts as a doctor` `a licensed doctor`
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a doctor` (`a licensed doctor who is` `the spouse`)
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a doctor` (`a licensed doctor who is` `the insured person`)

-- def 2: special diseases, with the acute nephritis carve-out.
#ASSERT `a special disease` `hepatitis`
#ASSERT `a special disease` `sinusitis`
#ASSERT `a special disease` `a disease or symptom of the blood-forming system`
#ASSERT NOT `a special disease` `acute nephritis needing emergency treatment`
#ASSERT `a special disease` `an acute flare of chronic nephritis`
#ASSERT NOT `a special disease` `another illness or injury`

-- def 4 and def 21: a hospital mainly for convalescence is not a hospital; a place mainly
-- treating mental disorders is not a "hospital" (def 4) but is a "medical facility" (def 21).
#ASSERT `counts as a hospital` `a hospital`
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a hospital` (`a place whose main activity is` `convalescence or rest` `, of traditional medicine:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a hospital` (`a place whose main activity is` `treating mental disorders` `, of traditional medicine:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `counts as a medical facility` (`a place whose main activity is` `treating mental disorders` `, of traditional medicine:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a medical facility` (`a place whose main activity is` `caring only for the elderly` `, of traditional medicine:` FALSE)

-- def 12: maternity care.
#ASSERT `maternity` `childbirth`
#ASSERT `maternity` `a complication of pregnancy`
#ASSERT NOT `maternity` `an illness`

-- def 11: obtaining the organ, and the donor's costs, are not insured.
#ASSERT `excluded by definition 11` `obtaining the organ, or the donor's costs`
#ASSERT NOT `excluded by definition 11` `an organ transplant`

-- defs 25, 27, 35: inpatient, day treatment, hospital stay ("more than 24 continuous
-- hours" or day treatment).
GIVEN hours     IS A NUMBER
      overnight IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A course of treatment`
`a formal admission of` hours `hours, overnight` overnight MEANS
    `a treatment built from` `inpatient treatment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) TRUE overnight hours `a hospital` `a licensed doctor` FALSE

#ASSERT `counts as inpatient treatment` (`a formal admission of` 30 `hours, overnight` TRUE)
#ASSERT `counts as day treatment` (`a formal admission of` 8 `hours, overnight` FALSE)
#ASSERT `counts as a hospital stay` (`a formal admission of` 25 `hours, overnight` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `counts as a hospital stay` (`a formal admission of` 24 `hours, overnight` TRUE)
#ASSERT `counts as a hospital stay` (`a formal admission of` 8 `hours, overnight` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `counts as inpatient treatment` (`an outpatient visit on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `counts as outpatient treatment` (`an outpatient visit on` (YMD 2026 3 1))

-- def 26: within 45 days after discharge; def 28: within 30 days before admission, or on
-- the day.
#ASSERT `within the 45 days after discharge` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT `within the 45 days after discharge` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 16)
#ASSERT NOT `within the 45 days after discharge` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `within the 30 days before admission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `within the 30 days before admission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `within the 30 days before admission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `within the 30 days before admission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 4 1)

-- def 30: a group policy is ten (10) or more.
#ASSERT `a group policy for a number of persons` 10
#ASSERT NOT `a group policy for a number of persons` 9

-- def 32: a follow-up visit counts as a new visit.
#ASSERT `the visits counted for` 1 `and` 2 EQUALS 3

-- def 34: two years from the last news; from the first of the next month, or of the next
-- year, if only the month or the year is known.
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`the day of the last news` (YMD 2026 3 5)) EQUALS YMD 2028 3 5
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`only the month` 3 2026) EQUALS YMD 2028 4 1
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`only the month` 12 2026) EQUALS YMD 2029 1 1
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`only the year` 2026) EQUALS YMD 2029 1 1

-- defs 36 and 38 (fork F1): continuous cover runs from the date first insured.
#ASSERT `the start date for` (`the renewing employee, continuously` TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT `the start date for` (`the renewing employee, continuously` FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the start date under definition 36 alone for` (`the renewing employee, continuously` TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1

